 δ, ∀ geodesic triangles, SideThin ...` (standard thin-triangles definition on the Cayley graph, hand-written, not a Mathlib notion).","gap":null,"note":"`main : ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), TorsionFree G ∧ WordHyperbolic G ∧ ¬ Group.ResiduallyFinite G` with `WordHyperbolic` = finite generating set whose Cayley graph has uniformly thin geodesic triangles (all three sides, `SideThin`). The summary's nonlinearity claim (one fixed element killed by every finite-dimensional representation over every commutative field) is not separately stated; it follows from the stated non-residual-finiteness via Mal'cev's theorem (docs: 'Nonlinearity over every field is not a separate conclusion').","reading":"reading:30cfcb74238c08eeb25e3ff3","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:f0eb4ebf9f7a1667532722db","reading:30cfcb74238c08eeb25e3ff3"],"state":"different-scope-descriptions"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750","repository":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine","source":"cert-machine","url":"https://carlostoledo.co/reports/openai-math.html"},"id":"reading:f0eb4ebf9f7a1667532722db","pair_review":false,"review_state":"outside-report","source":"cert-machine","source_term":"NARROWER — DECLARED","source_value":{"code":"NARROWER — DECLARED","confidence":"